{"name":"Tupelo Tree","hex":"#9c9152","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tupelo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several trees of the genus Nyssa which grow in swampy regions on the eastern, southern and midwestern United States.\nNyssa aquatica.\nNyssa multiflora, a North American tree of the dogwood family, with brilliant, glossy foliage and acid red berries.","Nyssa aquatica."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tupelo"},{"term":"tree","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A perennial woody plant taller and larger than a shrub with a wooden trunk and, at some distance from the ground, having leaves and branches.","Any other plant (such as a large shrub or herb) that is reminiscent of the above in form and size."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To chase (an animal or person) up a tree.","To place in a tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tree"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tupelo (tree)","blocks":[{"text":"Tupelo, genus Nyssa, is a small genus of deciduous trees with alternate, simple leaves. It is sometimes included in the subfamily Nyssoideae of the dogwood family, Cornaceae, but is placed by other authorities in the family Nyssaceae, as in the APG IV system."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Nyssa_sylvatica_flowers.jpg/330px-Nyssa_sylvatica_flowers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tupelo_(tree)","wikidata":"Q964952"},{"title":"Tree","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a tree is a perennial plant with an elongated stem, or trunk, usually supporting branches and leaves. In some usages, the definition of a tree may be narrower, e.g., including only woody plants with secondary growth, only plants that are usable for timber, or only plants above a specified height. Wider definitions include taller palms, tree ferns, bananas, and bamboos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree","wikidata":"Q10884"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/2014-11-02_12_47_05_Black_Tupelo_during_autumn_at_The_College_of_New_Jersey_in_Ewing%2C_New_Jersey.JPG/500px-2014-11-02_12_47_05_Black_Tupelo_during_autumn_at_The_College_of_New_Jersey_in_Ewing%2C_New_Jersey.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/2014-11-02_12_47_05_Black_Tupelo_during_autumn_at_The_College_of_New_Jersey_in_Ewing%2C_New_Jersey.JPG/1280px-2014-11-02_12_47_05_Black_Tupelo_during_autumn_at_The_College_of_New_Jersey_in_Ewing%2C_New_Jersey.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/2014-11-02_12_47_05_Black_Tupelo_during_autumn_at_The_College_of_New_Jersey_in_Ewing%2C_New_Jersey.JPG/500px-2014-11-02_12_47_05_Black_Tupelo_during_autumn_at_The_College_of_New_Jersey_in_Ewing%2C_New_Jersey.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nyssa sylvatica turning scarlet in autumn","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2014-11-02_12_47_05_Black_Tupelo_during_autumn_at_The_College_of_New_Jersey_in_Ewing%2C_New_Jersey.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/NyssaSylvaticaTrunk.jpg/500px-NyssaSylvaticaTrunk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/NyssaSylvaticaTrunk.jpg/1280px-NyssaSylvaticaTrunk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/NyssaSylvaticaTrunk.jpg/500px-NyssaSylvaticaT